# nginx-block-bad-ips whitelist: addresses here are ALWAYS allowed, even if a
# blocklist or a GeoIP rule would block them (the whitelist always wins).
#
# One IPv4/IPv6 address or CIDR per line. Comments start with #.
# After editing by hand run:  nginx-block-bad-ips apply
# Or use:                     nginx-block-bad-ips whitelist add 203.0.113.10
#
# Always allowed without being listed here: Cloudflare ranges, private and
# reserved ranges (10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16, 100.64/10, 127/8, ...),
# this server's own addresses and the trusted proxies from the configuration.
#
# This file is backed up to /root/ by uninstall.sh.
#
# Examples:
# 203.0.113.10        # office
# 198.51.100.0/24     # monitoring provider
# 2001:db8:1234::/48  # IPv6 office network
